# dead-code.allow — code this tree cannot reach today, and what will resolve it.
#
# RULES/17-no-dead-code.md. Two kinds of line, and neither is a deferral:
#
#   path/to/file    # consumer: <who reads it, outside this tree>
#   path/to/file    # ticket:<type>-<NNNN> — <what will resolve it>
#
# "we might need it later" is not a reason. A ticket line is a work queue with a date on it:
# closing the ticket DELETES the line, and the guard fails if a line outlives its code.
#
# First run, 2026-10-10 — five files, 327 scanned. Reported by the guard itself, not by hand.

